From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pixel5 <pixel5@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:11:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] LOCAL: media: venus: SM7250 encoder (CVP core, secure
 non-pixel PERSIST)

The IRIS1 encoder pre-processes every input frame (VPSS) on the CVP core,
vcodec1 (MVS1), so vcodec1 is now powered whenever vcodec0 is.

The CVP core reads its register-program table from the session's
INTERNAL_PERSIST buffer through the secure non-pixel stream ID (0x1384),
even in a non-secure session: downstream always allocates an encoder's
PERSIST buffer as CP_NON_PIXEL memory. With no context bank for that
stream the SoC freezes at the first frame and resets.

A "non-pixel" child node (iommus, qcom,iommu-vmid, memory-region) now gets
its own platform device and IOMMU domain. Its no-map carveout is handed to
the VM once and mapped once at an IOVA inside the content-protection
non-pixel range; encoder PERSIST buffers are carved from it with a
gen_pool. The context bank's page tables are shared with the VM by the
SMMU driver (local patch 0016). Without the bank the encoder is not
registered.

Measured on redfin (Tests 235-248, proof of concept): 1080p H.264 at about
150 fps with 1.2-1.4 s of CPU time for 300 frames.
